Considering motivations in decision-making**\n\nI’m reflecting on the complexities of full knowledge motivation, particularly how screens might indicate that K is not necessary. There seems to be a tension between the payoffs for defectors versus cooperators, like 10 vs. 0. I’m finding it interesting that the concept of conditional symmetry is related to marginal accuracy, but the role of selfish utilities doesn’t align with fairness enforcement. It appears pure policies may only work within a finite history and deterministic framework.","format":"openai-responses-v1","index":3},{"type":"reasoning.encrypted","data":"gAAAAABq8Pyv1YZP1aDDLDyVF8R-XjHF5Rnwmdgp2Tx3apV-fWpZhoc2TryBV2uA5BFQD3PG6nZxb23hcgZ90WJyz3wrxlm5frDqjcWccZq2Z-SAX2QI5IT2m_V3GcHTuT4ODm2MQ3Qy6Ts0jyfywXTF0QePgHjI07H_FqAKchSOvMv3e6AASMaTeRFLIhTJVBX15yop_1l_sNJLHokx5LBqPDuYW5a3fMQkQ-37DkC1CNbjRRHFh2i8OsyJrsAKeekiERw0UR-aiEqq9znorYnSQ4IBdBI1GISFWuqjIfBeRYOmlGxO_5PEf00g03z9v-SK2GhqVB8M-cwBvLJVIkzsemhLCqxCCV9OG1dXc8SsXWsY3HAp3JwPu7gDE6a-_WUoXPphUcdJIm3Szcya7HrREuMmkyN6ADcmaGqxFqse88jFrWhV4aq2pgWkITn3heTTde7jLWSjxxQ9m1J9CQQGoWchzcMYl5v67GNTEfT2rP5YMtY6aagbvBmQc4VPf9z3yaiUXZF8Nkzh20WVDLgKkfEywYj0EME37_1P24coHjUc1TR5P0E9KfWjg_kCNRptFrP160fG_SampfGJpVpHuxy_L01H8XwpBSHTg7jq0eOMj58CZkMEflBLYKfjxF4ZKE-7bx9_l_TttSawAwlcGw0nVN7ZPaC_qqKUHVrGtERqFYdfQR3NmmPmSddd4nV2Zs3kMg4cjqaCKufmpEFRqGogg3QB_YDMaTMgTaxGqvAMlTVHSgNiAW4Jlcu1PkBCTOTh3HcbYr2QJ_qc3VhuRyEfnhQDK14ET8l-QA-nwoOqggvbtvR_-Nn7QlxQHoUUoMZFLtDd8smwIDuvvcICCcSC4JsdlPgQ12jZGJ-9xPUiG-dvm1U3aDgJUK0wI8grOBecRxUEj88xBNxNNiIpUQCsBkQusuM_LWPYLqYY_08Kt2lbnnI7JWn-m1rrTpU1XVVL2BEKnJcbg7gyyKa9ivn976TNK7AD_ZV56tbOdlG43lHiM3yZHXg8r1HuY_JRBLWpO_25DQa8PbtuZIZFWWBZauRcPp3Sbfxl0BuOeGry7zLAzsLZSsRK4P7ojqhybmdOIk12JhGRYOU4xqFltMYRDXwp4syfXfToih79s-galvgeATtYblenyJ5uiwy1sxwvC-m2X-4bayj7W1b89k4YVp2Dugag3zrZ8GL5TCLQ6BxjTAtkfa9lvF3dSHexndx0yYqVI9lLNXMFgEU51k7WCHtn3LsWwhbpKBNHjnlqb_hPN1fO0MY_6OXfM7Lqf3dDdk-R8bRiA2wpTO_xm0fGMK4McO3w1Hb7O-KYHYFuRNvwxkwhYgTUXLAhZ7-KyEvNDXz08XDMEnVqIJv0Nm9ySsXf